      "uncited_sentences": [
        "The span detector architecture includes a multi-turn answer module.",
        "Formally, at time step $t$ in the range of $T$, the state is defined by $s_t = \text{tanh}(W_s [h_{t-1} || m_t] + b_s)$, where $h_{t-1}$ is the previous state and $m_t$ is the memory.",
        "The initial state $s_0$ is the summary of the memory: $s_0 = \text{tanh}(W_s m_0 + b_s)$, where $m_0$ is computed from the previous state and memory: $m_t = \text{tanh}(W_m [h_{t-1} || m_{t-1}] + b_m)$.",
        "Finally, a bilinear function is used to find the begin and end point of answer spans at each reasoning step: $score(h_t, m_t) = h_t^T W_s m_t$, where $W_s$ is a learnable weight matrix."
      ]
    }
  }
